  "id": "COMPOUND:2041 - PROTEIN:4276",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that K-252a may interact with Proto-oncogene tyrosine-protein kinase ROS through multiple indirect pathways. The first path links K-252a to Placenta growth factor, which is targeted by Gerontoisoflavone A, and Gerontoisoflavone A is known to target Proto-oncogene tyrosine-protein kinase ROS. The second path connects K-252a to Neutral amino acid transporter B(0), which is targeted by a complex compound that ultimately targets Proto-oncogene tyrosine-protein kinase ROS. The third path shows K-252a targeting ATP-citrate synthase, which is also targeted by a complex compound that leads to the same final target. These findings suggest that K-252a may act as a modulator of the activity of these targets, potentially through a common downstream effect on Proto-oncogene tyrosine-protein kinase ROS. The evidence supports a possible role for K-252a in influencing the activity of this kinase, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear.",
